## Phase 1 — Full wipe

```powershell
cd C:\Users\caoli\Documents\.Projects\.75-DAY-CHALLENGE\SIEM_SOC_AI_TOOL\wazuh-docker\single-node
docker compose down -v
docker system prune -a --volumes -f
```

- [ ] `docker ps -a` returns nothing
- [ ] `docker volume ls` returns nothing related to wazuh

---

## Phase 2 — Fix certs.yml BEFORE generating anything

```powershell
notepad config\certs.yml
```

Paste exactly this (note the `ip2` on the server node — this is what let agents
register by IP later):

```yaml
# note: changed all ip to 192.168.1.14
nodes:
  # Wazuh indexer server nodes
  indexer:
    - name: wazuh.indexer
      ip: 192.168.1.14

  # Wazuh server nodes
  # Use node_type only with more than one Wazuh manager
  server:
    - name: wazuh.manager
      ip: 192.168.1.14

  # Wazuh dashboard node
  dashboard:
    - name: wazuh.dashboard
      ip: 192.168.1.14
```

- [ ] Saved and closed

---

## Phase 3 — Generate certs (run PowerShell as Administrator)

```powershell
docker compose -f generate-indexer-certs.yml run --rm generator
```

- [ ] Output ends with all 4 "certificates created" lines
- [ ] Verify names are correct (NOT `demo.*`):
  ```powershell
  ls config\wazuh_indexer_ssl_certs\
  ```
  Should show `wazuh.indexer.pem`, `wazuh.manager.pem`, `wazuh.dashboard.pem`, `admin.pem`, `root-ca.pem` (+ `-key.pem` versions)

  if permission issue:
  ```powershell
  # Delete the folder entirely
  Remove-Item -Recurse -Force config\wazuh_indexer_ssl_certs
  # Recreate it fresh
  New-Item -ItemType Directory -Force -Path "config\wazuh_indexer_ssl_certs"
  ```
- [ ] Verify the manager cert has the IP SAN:
  ```powershell
  & "C:\Program Files\Git\usr\bin\openssl.exe" x509 -in "config\wazuh_indexer_ssl_certs\wazuh.manager.pem" -noout -text | findstr "IP Address"
  ```
  Should show both `192.168.1.9`
- [ ] Verify the indexer cert CN is correct:
  ```powershell
  & "C:\Program Files\Git\usr\bin\openssl.exe" x509 -in "config\wazuh_indexer_ssl_certs\wazuh.indexer.pem" -noout -subject
  ```
  Should show `CN=wazuh.indexer` (not `demo.indexer`)

**Do not proceed until both cert checks above pass.**

IF CERTS GENERATE WRONG, FOLLOW PHASE 4. IF NOT SKIP TO PHASE 5

---

## Phase 4 — Copy certs into place

```powershell
New-Item -ItemType Directory -Force -Path "config\certs"
New-Item -ItemType Directory -Force -Path "config\wazuh_manager\certs"
New-Item -ItemType Directory -Force -Path "config\wazuh_indexer\certs"
New-Item -ItemType Directory -Force -Path "config\wazuh_dashboard\certs"

Copy-Item "config\wazuh_indexer_ssl_certs\root-ca.pem" "config\certs\root-ca.pem" -Force

Copy-Item "config\wazuh_indexer_ssl_certs\wazuh.manager.pem" "config\wazuh_manager\certs\wazuh.manager.pem" -Force
Copy-Item "config\wazuh_indexer_ssl_certs\wazuh.manager-key.pem" "config\wazuh_manager\certs\wazuh.manager-key.pem" -Force

Copy-Item "config\wazuh_indexer_ssl_certs\wazuh.indexer.pem" "config\wazuh_indexer\certs\wazuh.indexer.pem" -Force
Copy-Item "config\wazuh_indexer_ssl_certs\wazuh.indexer-key.pem" "config\wazuh_indexer\certs\wazuh.indexer-key.pem" -Force
Copy-Item "config\wazuh_indexer_ssl_certs\admin.pem" "config\wazuh_indexer\certs\admin.pem" -Force
Copy-Item "config\wazuh_indexer_ssl_certs\admin-key.pem" "config\wazuh_indexer\certs\admin-key.pem" -Force

Copy-Item "config\wazuh_indexer_ssl_certs\wazuh.dashboard.pem" "config\wazuh_dashboard\certs\wazuh.dashboard.pem" -Force
Copy-Item "config\wazuh_indexer_ssl_certs\wazuh.dashboard-key.pem" "config\wazuh_dashboard\certs\wazuh.dashboard-key.pem" -Force
Copy-Item "config\wazuh_indexer_ssl_certs\root-ca.pem" "config\wazuh_dashboard\certs\root-ca.pem" -Force
```

- [ ] Verify every file is a real file (Length > 0, not a directory):
  ```powershell
  Get-ChildItem config\certs\, config\wazuh_manager\certs\, config\wazuh_indexer\certs\, config\wazuh_dashboard\certs\ | Select-Object Name, Mode, Length
  ```
  Every `Mode` should start with `-`, every `Length` > 0

**Do not proceed until every single cert file passes this check.**

