## Phase 5 — Start the stack

```powershell
docker compose up -d
```

- [ ] `docker compose ps` shows all 3 containers as `Up`

Open a second PowerShell window and watch the indexer:
```powershell
docker logs single-node-wazuh.indexer -f --tail 5
```

- [ ] Wait until you see repeating `.opendistro_security` errors (this means it's up and waiting — expected)

if need debugging: find opensearch
```powershell
docker compose exec wazuh.manager sh -c 'find /var/ossec -type f \( -name "*.pem" -o -name "*.key" \) -ls'
docker compose exec wazuh.manager sh -c 'find / -type f \( -name "*.pem" -o -name "*.key" \) 2>/dev/null'
```
---

## Phase 6 — Initialize security index

The moment you see the repeating errors above, run this in the FIRST window:

```powershell
docker exec -it single-node-wazuh.indexer bash -c "export JAVA_HOME=/usr/share/wazuh-indexer/jdk && bash /usr/share/wazuh-indexer/plugins/opensearch-security/tools/securityadmin.sh -cd /usr/share/wazuh-indexer/opensearch-security/ -nhnv -cacert /usr/share/wazuh-indexer/certs/root-ca.pem -cert /usr/share/wazuh-indexer/certs/admin.pem -key /usr/share/wazuh-indexer/certs/admin-key.pem -p 9200 -icl"
```

- [ ] Output ends with `Done with success`

---

## Phase 7 — Verify no more cert mismatch

```powershell
docker logs single-node-wazuh.manager --tail 15
```

- [ ] **No** `x509: certificate is valid for demo.indexer` errors
- [ ] Check data is actually flowing:
  ```powershell
  docker exec -it single-node-wazuh.manager bash -c "curl -k -u admin:SecretPassword https://wazuh.indexer:9200/wazuh-alerts-*/_count"

  # Check Filebeat
  docker exec -it single-node-wazuh.manager bash -c "filebeat test output"
  ```
  (If `curl: command not found`, that's fine — skip this specific check and rely on the dashboard instead)

**If you still see `demo.indexer` here, STOP. Do not continue to agents.**
Go back to Phase 3 and re-check the cert CN — something didn't regenerate.

