## Phase 9 — Set up the portproxy scheduled task (ONE TIME, before any agent)

```powershell
notepad C:\wsl-portproxy.ps1
```

Paste:
```powershell
Start-Sleep -Seconds 10
$wslIP = (wsl hostname -I).Trim().Split(" ")[0]
netsh interface portproxy delete v4tov4 listenport=1514 listenaddress=0.0.0.0
netsh interface portproxy delete v4tov4 listenport=1515 listenaddress=0.0.0.0
netsh interface portproxy add v4tov4 listenport=1514 listenaddress=0.0.0.0 connectport=1514 connectaddress=$wslIP
netsh interface portproxy add v4tov4 listenport=1515 listenaddress=0.0.0.0 connectport=1515 connectaddress=$wslIP
```

Register the task:
```powershell
$action = New-ScheduledTaskAction -Execute "PowerShell.exe" -Argument "-ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File C:\wsl-portproxy.ps1"
$trigger = New-ScheduledTaskTrigger -AtStartup
$settings = New-ScheduledTaskSettingsSet -AllowStartIfOnBatteries -DontStopIfGoingOnBatteries
Register-ScheduledTask -TaskName "WSL2PortProxy" -Action $action -Trigger $trigger -Settings $settings -RunLevel Highest -Force
```

Run it once now manually so it's active immediately:
```powershell
Start-ScheduledTask -TaskName "WSL2PortProxy"
Start-Sleep -Seconds 15
netsh interface portproxy show all
```

- [ ] Shows rules for both 1514 and 1515 pointing at current WSL2 IP

